{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H7PckXtxeJPRfPEJzJyugX","type":"tool_result","content":"0\t\n1\t## 输出风格\n2\t\n3\t- 回复简洁直接，不说废话\n4\t- 禁止客套开场（\"好的！\"、\"没问题！\"、\"这是个好问题！\"）和结束语（\"希望对你有帮助！\"、\"如果还有问题请随时问！\"）\n5\t- 不要复述用户的问题\n6\t- 不要给未被要求的建议或补充说明\n7\t- 推理要彻底，但输出只保留结论和必要信息\n8\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dcbc9989-a384-4059-b23d-1b456a845b92","uuid":"81e04399-ed7a-4cdf-8d78-cb31fbddb727","timestamp":"2026-05-14T18:47:17.236Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513/.claude/CLAUDE.md","content":"\n## 输出风格\n\n- 回复简洁直接，不说废话\n- 禁止客套开场（\"好的！\"、\"没问题！\"、\"这是个好问题！\"）和结束语（\"希望对你有帮助！\"、\"如果还有问题请随时问！\"）\n- 不要复述用户的问题\n- 不要给未被要求的建议或补充说明\n- 推理要彻底，但输出只保留结论和必要信息\n","numLines":9,"startLine":0,"totalLines":9}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Qwz9v1daoNEZyrqb3xxfNr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed predicted data for each experiment in the experiment_plan under the \"median\" tier definition. Let me carefully go through all experiments and generate predictions based on the median tier's core assumptions.\n\nLet me identify the two planned experiments:\n1. `gold-set` (status: planned) - Human-annotated 650 windows\n2. `f1-stag-analysis` (status: planned) - F1_stag per-class breakdown\n\nFor all DONE experiments, I need to generate \"imagined\" gold-set evaluation results under the median tier. But wait - the user says \"对 experiment_plan 中每个 planned 实验展开详细数据\". Let me re-read.\n\n\nSo they want me to generate detailed predicted data for each experiment in the experiment_plan. Most are DONE already, but I think they want predictions for the planned experiments (gold-set and f1-stag-analysis), plus imagined gold-set-contextualized results for the DONE experiments showing what would happen under median tier assumptions. Re-reading more carefully: \"对 experiment_plan 中每个 planned 实验展开详细数据\" - this means for each experiment with status \"planned\", I need to expand detailed predicted data with result_rationale for each prediction.\n\nThere are exactly 2 planned experiments: gold-set (the critical human annotation experiment) and f1-stag-analysis (F1_stag per-class breakdown). The median tier definition is specifically about what happens when gold set results come in, so gold-set is the primary one to predict. But I'm second-guessing whether \"planned 实验\" means just status=planned or all experiments in the plan. Given the Phase 1 context and median tier definition, I think the user wants predictions for all experiments in the experiment_plan, not just the ones with status=planned. I'm realizing the user wants predicted results for all planned experiments in the experiment_plan, which means generating comprehensive data for the gold-set annotation study and the F1_stag analysis, plus imagining how existing models would perform when re-evaluated against the gold standard. Let me structure this as a complete YAML output with detailed predictions across all these dimensions. Now I'm seeing that only the gold-set and f1-stag-analysis experiments are marked as planned, so I need to focus my predictions on just those two rather than all the experiments in the plan.\n\nFor the gold-set experiment specifically, I'm breaking down the median tier predictions: with 650 annotated windows, I'd expect inter-annotator agreement around 0.65, gold versus labeling function agreement at 0.61, and the labeling function accuracy varying by confidence level—around 0.80 for high-confidence labels and 0.50 for low-confidence ones. For the model evaluations on gold, the structural model should reach roughly 0.76 macro F1, the probe around 0.69, with about a 7-point gap between them.\n\nContinuing with the remaining gold-set metrics: the LLM judge would land around 0.61 macro F1 with roughly a 15-point gap versus the structural model, temporal onset alignment should be identifiable at about 52%, and there are semantic residuals—error patterns that neither the structural nor natural language approaches fully capture. For the F1 stagnation analysis, I'm looking at how performance breaks down across different stagnation subtypes to identify which patterns are particularly challenging.\n\nNow I'm structuring this as a comprehensive YAML output that captures both experiments with detailed result rationales explaining why each metric falls where it does. metrics that would appear in the actual experiment. I need to make these internally consistent.\n\nKey reasoning for median tier predictions:\n\n**Gold-LF kappa ~0.61**: LFs capture the direction of stagnation (cmd repetition, file diff stalling, outcome failure) but have systematic biases. cmd_rep fires too aggressively (we know from OH data), outcome_bp has temporal lag that creates boundary noise. Human annotators would recognize some stagnation that LFs miss (semantic stagnation) and disagree with some LF calls (boundary cases). κ=0.61 reflects \"substantial\" but not \"almost perfect\" agreement.\n\n**Conf≥2 accuracy ~0.80**: When 2+ LFs agree, they're usually right about the general direction, but boundary placement is noisy. 20% disagreement comes from: (a) edge cases where repetitive-looking behavior is actually exploratory, (b) semantic stagnation LFs don't capture, (c) timing boundary misalignment.\n\n**Conf=1 accuracy ~0.50**: Single-LF windows are essentially coin flips against human judgment. This makes sense because conf=1 means only 1 of 3 LFs fired, and that single LF could easily be wrong (especially cmd_rep with its high false positive tendency).\n\n**Structural GB on gold ~0.76**: Currently 0.9951 on LF labels. On gold, drops dramatically because structural features are LF-aligned by construction. Gold reveals cases where structural features predict stagnation but humans don't (agent doing repetitive but productive work) and vice versa (semantically stagnant but structurally diverse). Still outperforms probe because structural features capture the \"easy\" stagnation reliably.\n\n**Probe on gold ~0.69**: The probe model drops even more sharply from its 0.9055 LF-label performance because it relies heavily on semantic patterns that don't align with human judgment on boundary cases and productive repetition. because probe learned from LF-derived labels and inherits their biases, PLUS has additional generalization gap. However, probe might capture some semantic signal that structural features miss, narrowing the gap from 9pp (LF labels) to ~7pp (gold).\n\n**LLM-judge on gold ~0.61**: Currently 0.6625 on LF labels. The LLM-judge's disagreements with LF labels might partly reflect correct human-aligned judgments, but it also makes systematic errors around technical understanding and format sensitivity. Looking at the median tier estimates, it could range from 0.55 to 0.66, so I'll estimate around 0.60 on gold labels—roughly similar to its LF performance but slightly lower once gold reveals which disagreements were actually mistakes.\n\n**Structural minus LLM-judge on gold ~15pp**: That puts the gap at roughly 0.76 - 0.60 = 16pp.\n\n**Temporal onset alignment ~52%**: On gold labels, the LF-identified stagnation onset aligns with human judgment about half the time within ±2 steps. The other half shows misalignment because human judgment of when stagnation truly begins is inherently subjective, LF temporal dynamics have ±2-3 step noise, and some stagnation types have gradual rather than sharp onsets.\n\nFor the f1-stag-analysis breakdown by stagnation subtype, I'd expect repetitive command stagnation to show high F1 (0.85+) since structural features catch it well, while exploratory stagnation with diverse commands would be harder to pin down.\n\nNow I need to think about which experiments actually need detailed predictions. Looking back at the plan, only gold-set and f1-stag-analysis have planned status—everything else is already done. So I'm focusing on generating detailed median-tier predictions for just those two experiments.\n\nThe gold-set experiment is really a multi-faceted evaluation, so I should break it into logical sub-experiments. This will let me generate results across all three claims systematically. I'm also thinking through what outputs these experiments would actually produce—tables showing LF accuracy against gold labels, confusion matrices, performance comparisons across different model types, and temporal alignment visualizations for gold-set; plus F1 breakdowns by stagnation pattern and per-class heatmaps for f1-stag-analysis.\n\nNow I'm working through the specific numbers to make sure everything is internally consistent across the YAML output.\n\nFor the gold set itself, I'm setting it at 650 windows with 3 annotators providing 2 annotations per window. The inter-annotator agreement comes out to a Cohen's κ of 0.67, and I'm deriving gold labels from the majority vote with adjudication for disagreements. The distribution skews toward progress at about 60% versus 40% stagnation, which reflects the actual base rate and differs slightly from what the labeling functions produced. When comparing gold labels against the LF predictions, the overall accuracy is 0.72 with a κ of 0.61, but this varies significantly by confidence level—windows with confidence ≥2 hit 0.82 accuracy while confidence=1 windows drop to 0.51, and the confusion pattern shows the LF tends to overpredict stagnation in some cases while underpredicting it in others.\n\nNow looking at how different models perform on the gold set: the structural GB model achieves a macro F1 of 0.76 with strong performance on both classes, while the probe model lags at 0.69 macro F1, giving the structural approach a 7-point advantage. The LLM-judge performs notably worse at 0.60 macro F1, putting it 16 points behind the structural model. For temporal alignment, I'm seeing that only about a third of predictions fall within ±1 step of the true onset, though this improves to 52% within ±2 steps and 64% within ±3 steps, with a mean offset of 2.8 steps.\n\nDigging into the error patterns, I'm identifying three key semantic categories: agents often cycle through different commands while pursuing the same logical strategy (about 25% of false positives), sometimes they repeat commands that are actually productive like iterative debugging (30% of false negatives), and there's a semantic plateau effect where outputs look structurally different but are semantically similar, which accounts for about 20% of the stagnation cases the structural model misses. Now I'm thinking through how to organize the experimental results—I'll structure this as a series of nested experiments under the gold set: the annotation itself, validation of the logical form labels against gold, evaluation of all models on gold, and temporal dynamics validation.\n\nFor the remaining analysis, I should add the semantic residual analysis and per-class F1 breakdown. Rather than creating separate top-level entries, I'll keep the two main experiments from the plan (gold-set and f1-stag-analysis) but break gold-set into multiple descriptive sub-experiments, each referencing the same plan_id so they're clearly grouped together.\n\nNow I'm working through the actual numbers for the gold set annotation. I'm planning 650 total windows stratified by LF confidence—roughly 250 at confidence level 1, 350 at confidence 2 or higher (with about 50 at the maximum confidence), and 50 flagged windows from error analysis. With two annotators per window and a third for disagreements, the adjudicated labels should yield around 260 stagnation cases (40%) and 390 progress cases (60%). Then I need to calculate the LF performance on the high-confidence subset to establish a baseline—on those 350 windows, the LF should achieve about 82% accuracy, meaning roughly 287 correct predictions and 63 errors.\n\nLooking at the breakdown across confidence levels, the low-confidence windows (conf=1) are essentially random at 51% accuracy since only one LF fired, while the highest-confidence windows (conf=3) perform much better at 92% accuracy. The overall agreement between the gold labels and LF predictions gives me a Cohen's kappa around 0.61. When I train the structural model on the full gold set, I'm seeing a macro F1 of 0.76, which represents about a 23 percentage point drop from the LF's performance.\n\nThe key insight here is that the structural model was trained on LF-derived labels, so it essentially learned to replicate what the LFs would predict. When evaluated against gold labels, it performs similarly to how the LFs themselves would perform on gold—around the same accuracy level—because the structural model is fundamentally approximating the LF outputs rather than learning something fundamentally different. The ~20-30% disagreement between LFs and gold labels explains why the structural model's performance on gold is constrained by how well the LFs themselves agree with the gold standard.\n\nFor the probe, even though it also learned from LF labels, it's working through embeddings which allows it to capture some semantic patterns that go beyond the raw LF rules. This gives it a slight advantage over the structural model on gold labels, though still lower than its performance on LF labels, since it's partially picking up on signals that align with human judgment but not perfectly.\n\nThe LLM-judge is interesting because it was already performing worse on LF labels, so the gap between its LF and gold performance narrows less dramatically. Some of its disagreements with LF labels were actually closer to human judgment, which could push it up slightly, but it also has its own systematic biases that don't always match human preferences, so I'm estimating it stays around 0.60 on gold.\n\nNow I need to finalize all these estimates and write them out in YAML format, then move on to breaking down the F1 scores for the stagnation class by subcategories in the median tier.\n\nLooking at the derived test set, I can see how the probe performs across different stagnation patterns—repetitive commands are easiest to detect at 0.91 F1, while outcome-only stagnation is much harder at 0.72, and when multiple signals agree the performance jumps to 0.94. On the gold set, the patterns shift: repetitive commands drop to 0.78, and exploratory stagnation is particularly challenging at 0.48.\n\nNow I'm organizing the full evaluation structure into sections covering annotation agreement, labeling function validation, structural model performance, probe evaluation, LLM judge results, temporal alignment, error taxonomy, and per-class F1 breakdown—each with supporting rationale. I'll write this out as clean YAML.\n\nLet me verify the internal consistency: the gold set has 650 windows stratified across confidence levels, with about 41.5% stagnation and 58.5% progress after human annotation. This distribution differs from the labeling function baseline because the stratified sampling overweights higher-confidence windows which tend toward stagnation, and some confidence-1 windows the functions marked as progress are actually stagnation by human judgment. The labeling functions themselves show strong accuracy on the highest-confidence windows (92% with κ=0.83) but drop to 82% accuracy on mid-confidence windows (κ=0.62).\n\nFor the lower-confidence windows, I need to reconsider what the confidence metric actually represents—it's the number of labeling functions agreeing with the majority vote, so confidence-1 means just one function aligned with the majority while the other two split the opposite way. That explains the near-chance performance there (51% accuracy, κ=0.08), and overall across all 650 windows the functions achieve 72% accuracy with κ=0.61. are abstaining or there's a tie), so the signal is weak.\n\nLooking at the distribution across confidence levels—most windows cluster at conf=1, which tracks with how many have ambiguous signals from the labeling functions. The accuracy pattern is clear: higher confidence correlates with better performance against the gold set, ranging from near-random at conf=1 to very strong agreement at conf=3.\n\nNow I need to compile these numbers into the YAML output and figure out what to do about the probe component.\n\nThe models were trained on LF labels, so I don't need to retrain them—I just evaluate the existing ones against the gold test set. The gold set spans all confidence levels and represents an independent evaluation without circular bias, which is the whole point. Let me pull the structural model's performance metrics on the full 650 gold windows.\n\nActually, I'm realizing the model was trained on windows with confidence ≥2, so its performance will differ depending on the confidence level of the gold windows it's evaluated on. When I stratify the evaluation, the structural model performs much better on the high-confidence subset (around 82% macro F1) compared to the confidence=1 subset (around 67%), which makes sense since the labeling functions themselves are more accurate on high-confidence windows. The overall weighted performance comes to about 76%, and this pattern suggests the structural features are essentially learning the same biases as the labeling functions rather than discovering something fundamentally different.\n\nThe probe model shows a similar stratification—around 75% on high-confidence gold windows and 60% on confidence=1 windows, for an overall 69%—but it drops more sharply from its LF performance because it wasn't as tightly coupled to the labeling function outputs to begin with. The LLM-judge, meanwhile, doesn't show as much variation across confidence levels since it has no knowledge of the LF confidence scores, achieving around 60% overall with roughly equal performance on both subsets.\n\nNow I'm looking at how these gaps shift between the LF and gold settings. The structural advantage over the probe narrows from about 9 percentage points on LF labels down to 7 points on gold, which tracks with the expected range—structural features retain their dominance but lose some of their artificial alignment boost. Against the LLM-judge, the gap is much larger on LF (around 33 points) but compresses significantly on gold (down to 16 points), showing how much the judge's performance improves when evaluated against human annotations.\n\nFor the paper, I'm planning out the tables and figures: annotation statistics with inter-annotator agreement and confidence breakdowns, a heatmap showing annotator alignment, LF accuracy stratified by confidence level with a confusion matrix, a comparison of all four models on both label sets, and a temporal analysis of onset alignment across LF types.\n\nI'm also mapping out error taxonomy with a Venn diagram showing what each approach captures, plus an F1 breakdown by stagnation pattern type with a performance heatmap across models.\n\nNow I'm confident in the numbers and ready to finalize the output. I need to make sure each rationale thoroughly explains why the median tier produces these results and connects back to the core assumptions. There's also a semantic residual in the gold set—human-recognizable stagnation types that neither the structural nor NL probe approach handles well, and I should identify what those types are.\n\nI'm seeing three main categories: strategic dead-ends where the agent pursues a coherent but fundamentally wrong direction that only humans can recognize, implicit repetition where the agent paraphrases the same approach in different syntax so literal command matching misses it, and productive-looking exploration that generates lots of activity but is actually unfocused thrashing. These three types make up roughly 35% of the gold-labeled stagnation windows that neither approach captures effectively.\n\nNow I need to finalize the YAML with these details and think through the F1 breakdown experiment. The f1-stag-analysis would first run on the existing test set to break down stagnation into subtypes, then potentially on the gold set once available. I'm looking at how to break down the stagnation F1 scores more systematically—by where in the trajectory it occurs, what type of stagnation it is, confidence levels, and whether the trajectory eventually resolves. I already have error rates from prior analysis showing early detection is more accurate than middle-stage, and resolved trajectories have much lower error than unresolved ones. The f1-stag-analysis experiment would compute actual F1 metrics across these subcategories, and I'm predicting the pattern holds: early and late detection around 0.87-0.88, middle around 0.79, with command repetition dominance performing best around 0.90.\n\nNow I'm ready to write out the YAML configuration for all eight experiments—seven under the gold-set plan and the f1-stag-analysis as its own plan.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":331,"cache_read_input_tokens":43089,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":331},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dcbc9989-a384-4059-b23d-1b456a845b92","uuid":"206c266c-afcb-42d7-a2c3-98eee10b27d9"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Qwz9v1daoNEZyrqb3xxfNr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Gold set 确认 LF labels 大方向正确但含系统性偏差。Claim 1 需降级：从 \"stagnation signals ARE structural\"\n  改为 \"LF-approximated stagnation is structural; human-recognizable stagnation has additional semantic dimensions.\"\n  Structural features 仍是最佳 practical 选择（效率 + 跨域），但不再 claim 语义理解无价值——而是 claim 当前 NL 方法\n  尚未有效捕获语义残差。Claim 2 temporal dynamics 加 caveat：onset timing 是统计趋势（±2-3 步噪声），非精确预测。\n  Claim 3 不变。标题从 \"signals are structural\" 调整为 \"structural features dominate current approaches\"。\n  仍冲 EMNLP，contribution pitch 从 \"definitive finding\" 转为 \"strong empirical evidence with identified limitations\"。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ── gold-set 子实验 1: 标注质量与基本统计 ──\n  - name: \"gold-annotation-stats\"\n    plan_id: \"gold-set\"\n    description: >\n      650 窗口人工标注基本统计：IAA、标签分布、置信度分层覆盖。\n      2 名标注者 per window，第 3 人仲裁分歧。分层采样自 54809 总窗口。\n    expected_results:\n      total_windows: 650\n      sampling_strategy: \"stratified by LF confidence\"\n      conf1_sampled: 250\n      conf2_sampled: 340\n      conf3_sampled: 60\n      annotators: 3\n      annotators_per_window: 2\n      adjudication_method: \"3rd annotator on disagreements\"\n      inter_annotator_kappa: 0.67\n      inter_annotator_pct_agreement: 0.81\n      gold_stagnation_count: 270\n      gold_progress_count: 380\n      gold_stag_ratio: 0.415\n      lf_stag_ratio_same_sample: 0.335\n      annotation_time_per_window_min: 3.5\n      total_annotation_hours: 38\n    result_rationale: >\n      IAA κ=0.67（substantial agreement）反映 stagnation 判断的固有主观性：标注者对\"结构性重复\"（高一致）\n      和\"语义停滞\"（低一致）的认知不同。Gold stag 比例（41.5%）高于 LF 标注（33.5%），因为人类识别出\n      LFs 遗漏的语义停滞——agent 命令多样但逻辑循环。κ=0.67 落在 median 范围 [0.50, 0.72] 中偏高位，\n      反映标注者在 SE domain 有足够的 coding agent 经验来达成中等以上共识，但边界案例仍有分歧。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Gold Set Annotation Summary\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Total windows\", 650]\n          - [\"Inter-annotator κ\", 0.67]\n          - [\"Inter-annotator % agreement\", \"81%\"]\n          - [\"Gold stagnation ratio\", \"41.5%\"]\n          - [\"LF stagnation ratio (same sample)\", \"33.5%\"]\n          - [\"Adjudicated windows\", \"124 (19.1%)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Annotator agreement heatmap (2×2): 同意-stag, 同意-prog, A1=stag/A2=prog, A1=prog/A2=stag\"\n    analysis: >\n      Gold stag 比例显著高于 LF stag 比例（41.5% vs 33.5%），暗示 LFs 系统性漏报 stagnation——\n      即存在 LFs 判定 progress 但人类判定 stagnation 的窗口（语义停滞）。这为 Claim 1 降级提供直接证据。\n      IAA 分歧主要集中在两类：(1) agent 做了 edit 但 edit 无效（标注者对\"无效 edit\"的判定标准不一），\n      (2) agent 在长 trajectory 末期的\"探索性尝试\"是否算 progress。\n\n  # ── gold-set 子实验 2: LF 标签 vs Gold 验证 ──\n  - name: \"gold-lf-validation\"\n    plan_id: \"gold-set\"\n    description: >\n      LF 标签（MV）与 gold 标签的一致性分析，按置信度分层。\n      核心回答：LF labels 在多大程度上反映真实 stagnation？\n    expected_results:\n      overall_gold_lf_kappa: 0.61\n      overall_gold_lf_accuracy: 0.72\n      overall_gold_lf_precision_stag: 0.78\n      overall_gold_lf_recall_stag: 0.63\n      overall_gold_lf_f1_stag: 0.70\n      conf3_accuracy: 0.92\n      conf3_kappa: 0.83\n      conf3_n: 60\n      conf2_accuracy: 0.82\n      conf2_kappa: 0.62\n      conf2_n: 340\n      conf2_precision_stag: 0.84\n      conf2_recall_stag: 0.73\n      conf1_accuracy: 0.51\n      conf1_kappa: 0.08\n      conf1_n: 250\n      conf1_precision_stag: 0.55\n      conf1_recall_stag: 0.41\n      lf_fp_rate: 0.14\n      lf_fn_rate: 0.14\n      lf_fp_pattern: \"cmd_rep false firing on productive-but-repetitive debugging sequences\"\n      lf_fn_pattern: \"semantic stagnation with diverse commands — LFs see activity, humans see no progress\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      κ=0.61 反映 LFs 捕获 stagnation 方向正确但有系统性偏差。Conf≥2 accuracy=0.82 落在 median 范围\n      [0.72, 0.88] 中间偏高：2+ LFs 同意时方向通常对，但边界噪声导致 ~18% 错误。\n      Conf=1 accuracy=0.51 接近随机（median 范围 [0.42, 0.58]），因为单个 LF 信号不足以可靠判断——\n      尤其 cmd_rep 在 conf=1 中贡献最多但 FP 率最高。\n      LF recall_stag 偏低（0.63）是关键发现：LFs 系统性遗漏约 37% 的人类标注 stagnation，\n      这些遗漏即\"语义残差\"——结构特征看不到的停滞类型。\n      LF precision_stag 较高（0.78）说明 LFs 判定 stagnation 时大多数时候是对的，但过于保守。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: LF Label Accuracy vs Gold by Confidence\"\n        columns: [\"Confidence\", \"N\", \"Accuracy\", \"κ\", \"Precision_stag\", \"Recall_stag\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"conf=3\", 60, 0.92, 0.83, 0.94, 0.88]\n          - [\"conf=2\", 340, 0.82, 0.62, 0.84, 0.73]\n          - [\"conf=1\", 250, 0.51, 0.08, 0.55, 0.41]\n          - [\"Overall\", 650, 0.72, 0.61, 0.78, 0.63]\n      - name: \"Table: LF Error Confusion Matrix (Overall)\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"Gold=Stag\", \"Gold=Prog\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LF=Stag\", \"170 (TP)\", \"48 (FP)\"]\n          - [\"LF=Prog\", \"100 (FN)\", \"332 (TN)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar chart: LF accuracy by confidence level (correct/FP/FN 三色)\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: per-window LF confidence score vs gold agreement (binary)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Conf≥2 准确率 0.82 验证了论文在 LF-derived labels 上训练的合理性——高置信标签方向基本正确。\n      但 conf=1 接近随机（0.51）意味着 54809 窗口中 39408 个（72%）的标签质量极差。\n      这解释了为什么 probe 在 full data (probe-002, F1=0.847) 低于 conf≥2 only (probe-001, F1=0.906)：\n      conf=1 噪声拖低了训练质量。LF recall_stag=0.63 的系统性遗漏为 Claim 1 降级提供了核心论据。\n\n  # ── gold-set 子实验 3: Structural 模型在 gold 上评估 ──\n  - name: \"gold-structural-eval\"\n    plan_id: \"gold-set\"\n    description: >\n      将已训练的 structural GB/RF/LR 模型在 650 gold 标签窗口上评估。\n      核心回答：structural features 在真实标签上的性能 + circular eval 的真实影响。\n    expected_results:\n      test_set: \"gold 650 windows\"\n      structural_gb:\n        macro_f1: 0.76\n        accuracy: 0.78\n        f1_stag: 0.71\n        f1_prog: 0.81\n      structural_rf:\n        macro_f1: 0.74\n        accuracy: 0.77\n        f1_stag: 0.68\n        f1_prog: 0.80\n      structural_lr:\n        macro_f1: 0.73\n        accuracy: 0.76\n        f1_stag: 0.67\n        f1_prog: 0.79\n      by_gold_confidence:\n        conf_ge2:\n          structural_gb_macro_f1: 0.82\n          n: 400\n        conf1:\n          structural_gb_macro_f1: 0.67\n          n: 250\n      drop_from_lf_eval_pp: -21.9\n      circular_eval_inflation_pp: 21.9\n    result_rationale: >\n      Structural GB 从 LF-eval 的 0.9951 暴跌至 gold-eval 的 0.76（-21.9pp），直接量化了 circular evaluation\n      的膨胀效应。这是 median 档的核心预期：structural features ≈ LF inputs，所以在 LF labels 上近乎完美\n      是 artifact，但在 gold 上仍保持 0.76 说明结构信号有真实价值——不只是拟合 LF 规则。\n      0.76 落在 median 范围 [0.68, 0.83] 中间。Conf≥2 上 GB 表现更好（0.82）因为这些窗口 LF\n      本身 82% 正确，structural features 在这些\"LF 正确\"的子集上性能保持。\n      Conf=1 上 GB 降至 0.67 但仍高于 LF 自身准确率（0.51），说明 GB 学到了超越单 LF 规则的\n      smoother boundaries。RF 略低于 GB 因为 RF 的离散 splits 更容易过拟合 LF 的离散规则，\n      而 GB 的 gradient boosting 有更好的正则化泛化。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Structural Models on Gold vs LF Labels\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"LF-eval F1\", \"Gold-eval F1\", \"Δ (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Structural GB\", 0.9951, 0.76, -23.5]\n          - [\"Structural RF\", 0.9951, 0.74, -25.5]\n          - [\"Structural LR\", 0.9874, 0.73, -25.7]\n          - [\"Probe (GRU)\", 0.9055, 0.69, -21.6]\n          - [\"LLM-judge\", 0.6625, 0.60, -6.3]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: 每个模型在 LF-eval vs Gold-eval 上的 macro_f1（双色对比）\"\n      - \"Feature importance on gold: structural GB 的 top-10 features 对比 LF-eval 的 feature importance 变化\"\n    analysis: >\n      Circular eval 膨胀 ~22pp 是论文最重要的方法论发现之一。但 structural features 在 gold 上仍为最高分\n      （0.76 vs probe 0.69 vs LLM-judge 0.60），证明\"structural features dominate current approaches\"\n      这一降级后的 claim 成立。Feature importance 可能发生重排序：LF-eval 上 cmd_rep_ratio 最重要\n      （因为 cmd_rep LF 覆盖率 97.4%），但 gold-eval 上 file_diff 相关特征可能上升（因为 file activity\n      是更可靠的 cross-context 信号）。\n\n  # ── gold-set 子实验 4: Probe 在 gold 上评估 ──\n  - name: \"gold-probe-eval\"\n    plan_id: \"gold-set\"\n    description: >\n      GRU probe（probe_001 + multiseed + encoder variants）在 gold 标签上评估。\n      核心回答：embedding-based approach 在真实标签上的相对表现。\n    expected_results:\n      test_set: \"gold 650 windows\"\n      probe_001_qwen:\n        macro_f1: 0.69\n        accuracy: 0.72\n        f1_stag: 0.62\n        f1_prog: 0.76\n      probe_e5large:\n        macro_f1: 0.71\n        accuracy: 0.74\n        f1_stag: 0.65\n        f1_prog: 0.77\n      probe_bgem3:\n        macro_f1: 0.72\n        accuracy: 0.74\n        f1_stag: 0.66\n        f1_prog: 0.78\n      structural_minus_probe_gold_pp: 7\n      structural_minus_probe_lf_pp: 8.96\n      gap_narrowing_pp: 1.96\n      by_gold_confidence:\n        conf_ge2:\n          probe_001_macro_f1: 0.75\n        conf1:\n          probe_001_macro_f1: 0.61\n    result_rationale: >\n      Probe 从 LF-eval 0.9055 降至 gold-eval 0.69（-21.6pp）：probe 在 LF labels 上训练，\n      继承了 LF 偏差，gold 暴露了这些偏差。但 structural - probe gap 从 8.96pp（LF）缩窄到 7pp（gold），\n      落在 median 范围 [1, 8] 内。缩窄原因：probe 的 embedding 捕获了一些 structural features 无法编码的\n      语义信号（如 action 描述的语义相似度暗示逻辑循环），这些信号在 LF-eval 上被 circular eval 淹没，\n      但在 gold 上体现出微弱的额外价值。BGE-m3 在 gold 上表现最好（0.72 vs Qwen 0.69），\n      可能因为 BGE-m3 的多语言训练使其对 code-NL 混合文本的编码更鲁棒，捕获了更多 task-agnostic 语义信号。\n      但 7pp gap 仍然显著，证明\"structural features dominate current approaches\"成立。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Probe Variants on Gold Labels\"\n        columns: [\"Encoder\", \"LF-eval F1\", \"Gold-eval F1\", \"Δ vs Structural GB (gold)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-0.6B\", 0.9055, 0.69, \"-7pp\"]\n          - [\"E5-large-v2\", 0.9363, 0.71, \"-5pp\"]\n          - [\"BGE-m3\", 0.9413, 0.72, \"-4pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Encoder 比较 bar chart: 三个 encoder 在 LF-eval vs Gold-eval 上的 macro_f1\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: probe 预测概率 vs gold label，按 LF confidence 着色\"\n    analysis: >\n      Probe 在 gold 上表现弱于 structural（7pp gap），但 encoder 之间的排序反转值得注意：\n      LF-eval 上 Qwen/BGE/E5 差距小（±3.6pp），但 gold 上 BGE-m3 拉开优势。\n      这暗示 encoder 的泛化能力差异在 circular eval 中被压缩，gold 上才暴露。\n      Probe 的真实 contribution 不是超越 structural，而是提供 (a) end-to-end 部署路径，\n      (b) 在 conf=1 的语义歧义窗口上可能有互补价值（probe conf=1 F1=0.61 vs structural conf=1 F1=0.67，\n      差距仅 6pp，比 overall 差距 7pp 更小，暗示 probe 在歧义区域有相对优势）。\n\n  # ── gold-set 子实验 5: LLM-judge 在 gold 上评估 ──\n  - name: \"gold-llm-judge-eval\"\n    plan_id: \"gold-set\"\n    description: >\n      LLM-as-judge (Claude Sonnet, zero-shot) 在 gold 标签上评估。\n      核心回答：LLM-judge 对 LF labels 的\"disagreement\"中有多少是 correct human-aligned judgment？\n    expected_results:\n      test_set: \"gold 650 windows (same windows as LLM-judge baseline)\"\n      llm_judge_gold:\n        macro_f1: 0.60\n        accuracy: 0.63\n        f1_stag: 0.54\n        f1_prog: 0.66\n        precision_stag: 0.58\n        recall_stag: 0.50\n      llm_judge_lf_eval_ref:\n        macro_f1: 0.6625\n      delta_gold_vs_lf_pp: -6.3\n      structural_minus_llm_gold_pp: 16\n      probe_minus_llm_gold_pp: 9\n      llm_judge_correct_lf_wrong_pct: 8.2\n      llm_judge_wrong_lf_correct_pct: 14.5\n      llm_judge_both_wrong_pct: 6.1\n      by_gold_confidence:\n        conf_ge2:\n          llm_judge_macro_f1: 0.63\n        conf1:\n          llm_judge_macro_f1: 0.57\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLM-judge 从 LF-eval 0.6625 降至 gold-eval 0.60（-6.3pp），降幅远小于 structural（-22pp）\n      和 probe（-22pp）。这是因为 LLM-judge 本来就不拟合 LF labels，所以 circular eval 的去除\n      对它影响最小。但 LLM-judge 仍排最末（0.60），因为 zero-shot prompting 缺乏：\n      (a) 对 SWE-bench task 结构的先验知识（不知道什么 command pattern 意味着停滞），\n      (b) 窗口级时序 context（只看 5 步摘要，不理解 trajectory 动态），\n      (c) agent 架构特异性（不了解 SWE-Agent vs OpenHands 的行为模式）。\n      8.2% 的窗口上 LLM-judge 对而 LF 错——这些是 LLM 的\"语义理解\"正确捕获的案例，\n      但 14.5% 上 LLM 错而 LF 对，说明 LLM 的独立判断不够可靠。\n      Structural - LLM gap = 16pp 落在 median 范围 [5, 20] 中间，\n      证明 structural efficiency advantage survives 但 accuracy advantage 确实 weakens\n      （从 LF-eval 的 33pp 降到 gold 的 16pp）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: LLM-Judge Error Decomposition vs LF on Gold\"\n        columns: [\"Category\", \"Count\", \"% of 650\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Both correct\", 398, \"61.2%\"]\n          - [\"LLM correct, LF wrong\", 53, \"8.2%\"]\n          - [\"LLM wrong, LF correct\", 94, \"14.5%\"]\n          - [\"Both wrong\", 40, \"6.1%\"]\n          - [\"Ambiguous (adjudicated)\", 65, \"10.0%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: Structural vs Probe vs LLM-judge on gold macro_f1, 标注与 LF-eval 的 Δ\"\n      - \"Venn diagram: 三种方法在 gold 上的 correct predictions 重叠\"\n    analysis: >\n      LLM-judge \"correct but LF wrong\" 的 8.2% 窗口是宝贵的分析材料——这些是语义理解真正有价值的案例。\n      定性分析预期：这些窗口中 agent 在做\"看似活跃但语义空转\"的操作（多样命令、有 file edit，\n      但 edit 内容无效）。LLM 能读懂 edit 内容判断无效，而 LF 只看结构特征判定 progress。\n      然而 14.5% 的 \"LLM wrong, LF correct\" 表明 LLM 也有系统性偏差：\n      倾向于将 verbose output（长 error messages、详细 traceback）误判为 stagnation。\n\n  # ── gold-set 子实验 6: 时序动态在 gold 上的验证 ──\n  - name: \"gold-temporal-validation\"\n    plan_id: \"gold-set\"\n    description: >\n      在 gold 标注的 stagnation onset 边界上验证 LF temporal dynamics。\n      人类标注 stagnation 起始步，与 LF first-fire 步进行对齐分析。\n    expected_results:\n      gold_annotated_onsets: 270\n      onset_alignment:\n        within_1_step_pct: 32\n        within_2_steps_pct: 52\n        within_3_steps_pct: 64\n        mean_absolute_offset_steps: 2.8\n        median_absolute_offset_steps: 2.0\n        std_offset_steps: 2.1\n      by_lf:\n        cmd_rep:\n          mean_offset_vs_gold: -1.2\n          within_2_steps_pct: 48\n          note: \"fires before human-perceived onset, moderate alignment\"\n        file_diff:\n          mean_offset_vs_gold: -0.6\n          within_2_steps_pct: 56\n          note: \"most aligned with human onset, slightly early\"\n        outcome_bp:\n          mean_offset_vs_gold: 5.3\n          within_2_steps_pct: 22\n          note: \"fires well after human-perceived onset, by design\"\n      role_reversal_on_gold: >\n        Gold confirms cmd_rep leads on SWE-Agent (offset -1.2 vs gold) but temporal \n        role reversal on OH cannot be validated (no OH gold set in this batch).\n      onset_timing_noise_caveat: \"±2-3 step noise in onset alignment\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Overall onset alignment 52%（±2 步内）落在 median 范围 [40, 65] 中间。\n      低于 65% 因为：(a) 人类判断的 stagnation onset 本质是主观的（\"从哪一步开始不 productive\"\n      没有客观答案），(b) LFs 的 binary firing 是 threshold-based 的离散跳变，而人类感知的\n      onset 是渐进的，(c) OB（lagging LF）在 stagnation 已经发生很久后才 fire，拉低 average。\n      高于 40% 因为 cmd_rep 和 file_diff 作为 leading LFs，在多数 structural stagnation 案例上\n      确实在人类感知 onset 附近 fire。file_diff 对齐最好（56% within ±2），因为\"文件不再变化\"\n      是人类和 LF 共同认可的最直观 stagnation 信号。这支持 Claim 2 但需要加 caveat：\n      onset timing 是统计趋势（±2-3 步），不是精确预测工具。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: LF Onset Alignment with Gold Annotations\"\n        columns: [\"LF\", \"Mean Offset (steps)\", \"Within ±2 steps\", \"Within ±3 steps\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"cmd_rep\", -1.2, \"48%\", \"61%\"]\n          - [\"file_diff\", -0.6, \"56%\", \"68%\"]\n          - [\"outcome_bp\", +5.3, \"22%\", \"34%\"]\n          - [\"Any LF (first fire)\", -0.8, \"52%\", \"64%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Histogram: onset offset distribution (gold - LF first fire), 分 LF 着色\"\n      - \"Timeline visualization: 5 个 example trajectories 展示 gold onset vs LF fire 时间\"\n    analysis: >\n      cmd_rep 在 LF-eval 上 mean_lag=-1.87（relative to stag label onset），在 gold 上 offset=-1.2\n      （relative to human onset）——方向一致但幅度缩小。这是因为 LF-derived onset 定义比 human onset\n      更 sharp（binary threshold），而 gold onset 更渐进。\n      OB 在 gold 上 offset=+5.3（vs LF-eval 上 +6.7），缩小因为 gold-defined stagnation windows\n      通常更长（人类标注的 stagnation 包含了 LFs 未标记的\"尾部\"）。\n      关键 caveat：52% 的 ±2 步对齐意味着 onset prediction 只是粗略指示，不适合作为 intervention trigger。\n\n  # ── gold-set 子实验 7: 语义残差与错误分类学 ──\n  - name: \"gold-error-taxonomy\"\n    plan_id: \"gold-set\"\n    description: >\n      Gold set error analysis：识别 structural features 和 probe 都无法捕获的 stagnation 类型\n      （\"语义残差\"），构建 stagnation 类型分类学。\n    expected_results:\n      total_gold_stagnation: 270\n      structural_correct_stag: 192\n      structural_missed_stag: 78\n      structural_recall_stag: 0.71\n      missed_stag_taxonomy:\n        strategic_dead_end:\n          count: 31\n          pct_of_missed: 39.7\n          description: >\n            Agent 追求连贯但根本错误的方法。命令多样、有 file edit，但方向错误。\n            只有理解 task goal 的人才能判断。cmd_rep 不 fire（命令不重复），\n            file_diff 不 fire（确实在改文件），OB 可能 fire 也可能不 fire。\n          structural_f1: 0.22\n          probe_f1: 0.28\n          llm_judge_f1: 0.38\n        implicit_repetition:\n          count: 24\n          pct_of_missed: 30.8\n          description: >\n            Agent 用不同语法/命令表达相同逻辑尝试。字面 cmd_rep 低，但语义重复高。\n            如：先 grep 搜索，再 find 搜索，再 ag 搜索——命令不同但意图相同。\n          structural_f1: 0.31\n          probe_f1: 0.35\n          llm_judge_f1: 0.33\n        unfocused_exploration:\n          count: 23\n          pct_of_missed: 29.5\n          description: >\n            Agent 快速切换多种方法但都不 viable。结构上看像 productive exploration\n            （命令多样、文件变化频繁），但实际是无方向的 thrashing。\n          structural_f1: 0.18\n          probe_f1: 0.24\n          llm_judge_f1: 0.30\n      semantic_residual_total: 78\n      semantic_residual_pct_of_gold_stag: 28.9\n      probe_captures_partial_pct: 12.3\n      llm_captures_partial_pct: 18.7\n      neither_captures_pct: 22.6\n    result_rationale: >\n      78/270（28.9%）的 gold stagnation 构成\"语义残差\"——structural features 系统性 miss。\n      这些 stagnation 类型有共同特征：结构信号看起来像 progress（命令多样、有 file edit、\n      不触发 LF 阈值）。三种子类型反映不同的失败模式：\n      (1) strategic_dead_end（39.7%）是最大类：agent 一条路走到黑，结构上完全正常，\n      只有理解 task intent 才能判断。LLM-judge 在这类上最好（0.38）因为它能部分理解 intent；\n      (2) implicit_repetition（30.8%）：语义层面的重复，但 cmd_rep LF 的 literal matching 抓不到。\n      Probe embedding 理论上能捕获语义相似度但实际没有，因为 embedding 编码的是 step-level 文本\n      而非 action-level intent；\n      (3) unfocused_exploration（29.5%）：结构特征最难的一类，因为高活跃度被误判为 progress。\n      28.9% 的语义残差为 Claim 1 降级提供精确量化：structural features 捕获 71% 的真实 stagnation，\n      但遗漏 29%。这不是 marginal gap——是结构方法论的固有 ceiling。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Stagnation Type Taxonomy on Gold Set\"\n        columns: [\"Type\", \"Count\", \"% of Gold Stag\", \"Struct F1\", \"Probe F1\", \"LLM F1\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Repetitive-structural (LFs capture)\", 146, \"54.1%\", 0.88, 0.79, 0.58]\n          - [\"Low-activity stagnation (LFs capture)\", 46, \"17.0%\", 0.83, 0.72, 0.55]\n          - [\"Strategic dead-end (semantic)\", 31, \"11.5%\", 0.22, 0.28, 0.38]\n          - [\"Implicit repetition (semantic)\", 24, \"8.9%\", 0.31, 0.35, 0.33]\n          - [\"Unfocused exploration (semantic)\", 23, \"8.5%\", 0.18, 0.24, 0.30]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: stagnation type × method performance (structural / probe / LLM)\"\n      - \"Example windows: 每种 semantic residual 类型展示 1-2 个代表性 trajectory 片段\"\n      - \"Venn diagram: structural / probe / LLM 在 gold stagnation 上的 coverage overlap\"\n    analysis: >\n      语义残差的存在证明 Claim 1 的原始表述（\"signals ARE structural\"）过强。修正为：\n      \"LF-approximated stagnation 是 structural 的；但 human-recognizable stagnation 有额外的\n      语义维度，当前所有自动方法（structural、NL probe、LLM-judge）都未有效捕获。\"\n      重要的是：probe 和 LLM-judge 在语义残差上也表现很差（F1 0.24-0.38），说明当前 NL 方法\n      同样无法捕获语义残差——这支持\"structural features dominate CURRENT approaches\"的降级 claim，\n      同时为 future work 打开空间（需要 task-aware semantic understanding）。\n\n  # ── f1-stag-analysis ──\n  - name: \"f1-stag-per-class-breakdown\"\n    plan_id: \"f1-stag-analysis\"\n    description: >\n      在现有 LF-derived test set (N=1824) 上对 F1_stag 按多维度拆分：\n      trajectory 位置、dominant LF、置信度、trajectory outcome。\n      补充 gold set 上的同维度拆分（如可用）。\n    expected_results:\n      test_set_lf: \"conf≥2, N=1824, 485 stag / 1339 prog\"\n      overall_f1_stag: 0.8593\n      by_trajectory_position:\n        early_0_33:\n          n_stag: 98\n          f1_stag: 0.88\n          note: \"stagnation in early trajectory = usually clear repetitive pattern\"\n        middle_33_66:\n          n_stag: 132\n          f1_stag: 0.79\n          note: \"hardest segment — transitional states, boundary ambiguity\"\n        late_66_100:\n          n_stag: 255\n          f1_stag: 0.87\n          note: \"late stagnation usually well-established pattern\"\n      by_dominant_lf:\n        cmd_rep_dominant:\n          n_stag: 291\n          f1_stag: 0.90\n          note: \"cmd_rep signal strong and clean, probe easily learns\"\n        file_diff_dominant:\n          n_stag: 108\n          f1_stag: 0.83\n          note: \"file inactivity signal moderate, some false negatives\"\n        ob_dominant:\n          n_stag: 42\n          f1_stag: 0.72\n          note: \"OB-only stagnation hardest — lagging signal creates boundary noise\"\n        multi_signal:\n          n_stag: 44\n          f1_stag: 0.94\n          note: \"all LFs agree — easiest cases\"\n      by_confidence:\n        conf2:\n          n_stag: 463\n          f1_stag: 0.86\n        conf3:\n          n_stag: 22\n          f1_stag: 0.91\n      by_trajectory_outcome:\n        resolved:\n          n_stag: 8\n          f1_stag: 0.94\n          note: \"resolved trajectories have clear stag→progress transition\"\n        unresolved:\n          n_stag: 477\n          f1_stag: 0.85\n      gold_set_breakdown_if_available:\n        overall_f1_stag_gold: 0.62\n        by_type:\n          structural_stagnation: 0.78\n          semantic_stagnation: 0.27\n        by_position:\n          early: 0.68\n          middle: 0.55\n          late: 0.64\n    result_rationale: >\n      F1_stag 拆分揭示 probe 性能的非均匀分布。Middle segment 最差（0.79）因为 trajectory 中段\n      经常出现\"尝试新方向\"vs\"继续停滞\"的模糊过渡，probe 的 window-level 分类无法准确捕获\n      这种渐变。cmd_rep-dominant stagnation 最容易（0.90），因为 embedding 中的 token repetition\n      pattern 最易被 GRU 学习。OB-dominant 最难（0.72）因为 OB 是 lagging signal，\n      stagnation window 的 OB fire 来自未来的 outcome 信息，probe 在 inference 时看不到 outcome。\n      Multi-signal stagnation 最高（0.94）因为 all-3-agree 的窗口标签最干净、pattern 最一致。\n      Gold set 上 overall F1_stag 预期 0.62，远低于 LF-eval 的 0.86——semantic stagnation\n      类型（F1=0.27）大幅拉低整体。这是 Claim 1 降级的具体量化证据。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: F1_stag Breakdown by Dimension (LF Test Set)\"\n        columns: [\"Dimension\", \"Subcategory\", \"N_stag\", \"F1_stag\", \"Δ vs Overall\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Position\", \"Early (0-33%)\", 98, 0.88, \"+2.1pp\"]\n          - [\"Position\", \"Middle (33-66%)\", 132, 0.79, \"-6.9pp\"]\n          - [\"Position\", \"Late (66-100%)\", 255, 0.87, \"+1.1pp\"]\n          - [\"Dominant LF\", \"cmd_rep\", 291, 0.90, \"+4.1pp\"]\n          - [\"Dominant LF\", \"file_diff\", 108, 0.83, \"-2.9pp\"]\n          - [\"Dominant LF\", \"outcome_bp\", 42, 0.72, \"-13.9pp\"]\n          - [\"Dominant LF\", \"multi-signal\", 44, 0.94, \"+8.1pp\"]\n          - [\"Outcome\", \"Resolved\", 8, 0.94, \"+8.1pp\"]\n          - [\"Outcome\", \"Unresolved\", 477, 0.85, \"-0.9pp\"]\n      - name: \"Table: F1_stag on Gold by Stagnation Type (if gold available)\"\n        columns: [\"Stagnation Type\", \"N\", \"Probe F1_stag\", \"Structural F1_stag\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Structural (LF-capturable)\", 192, 0.78, 0.88]\n          - [\"Strategic dead-end\", 31, 0.22, 0.16]\n          - [\"Implicit repetition\", 24, 0.30, 0.25]\n          - [\"Unfocused exploration\", 23, 0.19, 0.12]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: F1_stag across position × dominant-LF (2D grid，颜色深浅表示 F1)\"\n      - \"Box plot: per-trajectory F1_stag 分布，按 trajectory outcome 分组\"\n      - \"Bar chart: LF-eval F1_stag vs Gold-eval F1_stag 对比（如 gold 可用）\"\n    analysis: >\n      F1_stag 的维度拆分提供三个关键 insights：\n      (1) OB-dominant stagnation（F1=0.72）是最大 weakness——这些窗口的 stagnation 信号\n      主要来自未来的 task outcome 而非当前 window 内容，probe 在 real-time inference 中无法利用；\n      (2) Middle-segment 低 F1（0.79）揭示 window-level 分类的固有局限：\n      stagnation onset/offset 的渐变过渡被 binary classification 强制离散化；\n      (3) Gold set 上的拆分（如可用）将把 structural vs semantic stagnation 的性能差距\n      精确量化：structural stagnation F1=0.78 vs semantic stagnation F1=0.27，\n      确认 ~29% 的 stagnation 是当前方法论的 blind spot。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":331,"cache_read_input_tokens":43089,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":331},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"dcbc9989-a384-4059-b23d-1b456a845b92","uuid":"269cc082-c80b-4341-8bcb-08ed83fdf0ab"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":401665,"duration_api_ms":403845,"num_turns":2,"result":"```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Gold set 确认 LF labels 大方向正确但含系统性偏差。Claim 1 需降级：从 \"stagnation signals ARE structural\"\n  改为 \"LF-approximated stagnation is structural; human-recognizable stagnation has additional semantic dimensions.\"\n  Structural features 仍是最佳 practical 选择（效率 + 跨域），但不再 claim 语义理解无价值——而是 claim 当前 NL 方法\n  尚未有效捕获语义残差。Claim 2 temporal dynamics 加 caveat：onset timing 是统计趋势（±2-3 步噪声），非精确预测。\n  Claim 3 不变。标题从 \"signals are structural\" 调整为 \"structural features dominate current approaches\"。\n  仍冲 EMNLP，contribution pitch 从 \"definitive finding\" 转为 \"strong empirical evidence with identified limitations\"。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  # ── gold-set 子实验 1: 标注质量与基本统计 ──\n  - name: \"gold-annotation-stats\"\n    plan_id: \"gold-set\"\n    description: >\n      650 窗口人工标注基本统计：IAA、标签分布、置信度分层覆盖。\n      2 名标注者 per window，第 3 人仲裁分歧。分层采样自 54809 总窗口。\n    expected_results:\n      total_windows: 650\n      sampling_strategy: \"stratified by LF confidence\"\n      conf1_sampled: 250\n      conf2_sampled: 340\n      conf3_sampled: 60\n      annotators: 3\n      annotators_per_window: 2\n      adjudication_method: \"3rd annotator on disagreements\"\n      inter_annotator_kappa: 0.67\n      inter_annotator_pct_agreement: 0.81\n      gold_stagnation_count: 270\n      gold_progress_count: 380\n      gold_stag_ratio: 0.415\n      lf_stag_ratio_same_sample: 0.335\n      annotation_time_per_window_min: 3.5\n      total_annotation_hours: 38\n    result_rationale: >\n      IAA κ=0.67（substantial agreement）反映 stagnation 判断的固有主观性：标注者对\"结构性重复\"（高一致）\n      和\"语义停滞\"（低一致）的认知不同。Gold stag 比例（41.5%）高于 LF 标注（33.5%），因为人类识别出\n      LFs 遗漏的语义停滞——agent 命令多样但逻辑循环。κ=0.67 落在 median 范围 [0.50, 0.72] 中偏高位，\n      反映标注者在 SE domain 有足够的 coding agent 经验来达成中等以上共识，但边界案例仍有分歧。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Gold Set Annotation Summary\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Total windows\", 650]\n          - [\"Inter-annotator κ\", 0.67]\n          - [\"Inter-annotator % agreement\", \"81%\"]\n          - [\"Gold stagnation ratio\", \"41.5%\"]\n          - [\"LF stagnation ratio (same sample)\", \"33.5%\"]\n          - [\"Adjudicated windows\", \"124 (19.1%)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Annotator agreement heatmap (2×2): 同意-stag, 同意-prog, A1=stag/A2=prog, A1=prog/A2=stag\"\n    analysis: >\n      Gold stag 比例显著高于 LF stag 比例（41.5% vs 33.5%），暗示 LFs 系统性漏报 stagnation——\n      即存在 LFs 判定 progress 但人类判定 stagnation 的窗口（语义停滞）。这为 Claim 1 降级提供直接证据。\n      IAA 分歧主要集中在两类：(1) agent 做了 edit 但 edit 无效（标注者对\"无效 edit\"的判定标准不一），\n      (2) agent 在长 trajectory 末期的\"探索性尝试\"是否算 progress。\n\n  # ── gold-set 子实验 2: LF 标签 vs Gold 验证 ──\n  - name: \"gold-lf-validation\"\n    plan_id: \"gold-set\"\n    description: >\n      LF 标签（MV）与 gold 标签的一致性分析，按置信度分层。\n      核心回答：LF labels 在多大程度上反映真实 stagnation？\n    expected_results:\n      overall_gold_lf_kappa: 0.61\n      overall_gold_lf_accuracy: 0.72\n      overall_gold_lf_precision_stag: 0.78\n      overall_gold_lf_recall_stag: 0.63\n      overall_gold_lf_f1_stag: 0.70\n      conf3_accuracy: 0.92\n      conf3_kappa: 0.83\n      conf3_n: 60\n      conf2_accuracy: 0.82\n      conf2_kappa: 0.62\n      conf2_n: 340\n      conf2_precision_stag: 0.84\n      conf2_recall_stag: 0.73\n      conf1_accuracy: 0.51\n      conf1_kappa: 0.08\n      conf1_n: 250\n      conf1_precision_stag: 0.55\n      conf1_recall_stag: 0.41\n      lf_fp_rate: 0.14\n      lf_fn_rate: 0.14\n      lf_fp_pattern: \"cmd_rep false firing on productive-but-repetitive debugging sequences\"\n      lf_fn_pattern: \"semantic stagnation with diverse commands — LFs see activity, humans see no progress\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      κ=0.61 反映 LFs 捕获 stagnation 方向正确但有系统性偏差。Conf≥2 accuracy=0.82 落在 median 范围\n      [0.72, 0.88] 中间偏高：2+ LFs 同意时方向通常对，但边界噪声导致 ~18% 错误。\n      Conf=1 accuracy=0.51 接近随机（median 范围 [0.42, 0.58]），因为单个 LF 信号不足以可靠判断——\n      尤其 cmd_rep 在 conf=1 中贡献最多但 FP 率最高。\n      LF recall_stag 偏低（0.63）是关键发现：LFs 系统性遗漏约 37% 的人类标注 stagnation，\n      这些遗漏即\"语义残差\"——结构特征看不到的停滞类型。\n      LF precision_stag 较高（0.78）说明 LFs 判定 stagnation 时大多数时候是对的，但过于保守。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: LF Label Accuracy vs Gold by Confidence\"\n        columns: [\"Confidence\", \"N\", \"Accuracy\", \"κ\", \"Precision_stag\", \"Recall_stag\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"conf=3\", 60, 0.92, 0.83, 0.94, 0.88]\n          - [\"conf=2\", 340, 0.82, 0.62, 0.84, 0.73]\n          - [\"conf=1\", 250, 0.51, 0.08, 0.55, 0.41]\n          - [\"Overall\", 650, 0.72, 0.61, 0.78, 0.63]\n      - name: \"Table: LF Error Confusion Matrix (Overall)\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"Gold=Stag\", \"Gold=Prog\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"LF=Stag\", \"170 (TP)\", \"48 (FP)\"]\n          - [\"LF=Prog\", \"100 (FN)\", \"332 (TN)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Stacked bar chart: LF accuracy by confidence level (correct/FP/FN 三色)\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: per-window LF confidence score vs gold agreement (binary)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Conf≥2 准确率 0.82 验证了论文在 LF-derived labels 上训练的合理性——高置信标签方向基本正确。\n      但 conf=1 接近随机（0.51）意味着 54809 窗口中 39408 个（72%）的标签质量极差。\n      这解释了为什么 probe 在 full data (probe-002, F1=0.847) 低于 conf≥2 only (probe-001, F1=0.906)：\n      conf=1 噪声拖低了训练质量。LF recall_stag=0.63 的系统性遗漏为 Claim 1 降级提供了核心论据。\n\n  # ── gold-set 子实验 3: Structural 模型在 gold 上评估 ──\n  - name: \"gold-structural-eval\"\n    plan_id: \"gold-set\"\n    description: >\n      将已训练的 structural GB/RF/LR 模型在 650 gold 标签窗口上评估。\n      核心回答：structural features 在真实标签上的性能 + circular eval 的真实影响。\n    expected_results:\n      test_set: \"gold 650 windows\"\n      structural_gb:\n        macro_f1: 0.76\n        accuracy: 0.78\n        f1_stag: 0.71\n        f1_prog: 0.81\n      structural_rf:\n        macro_f1: 0.74\n        accuracy: 0.77\n        f1_stag: 0.68\n        f1_prog: 0.80\n      structural_lr:\n        macro_f1: 0.73\n        accuracy: 0.76\n        f1_stag: 0.67\n        f1_prog: 0.79\n      by_gold_confidence:\n        conf_ge2:\n          structural_gb_macro_f1: 0.82\n          n: 400\n        conf1:\n          structural_gb_macro_f1: 0.67\n          n: 250\n      drop_from_lf_eval_pp: -21.9\n      circular_eval_inflation_pp: 21.9\n    result_rationale: >\n      Structural GB 从 LF-eval 的 0.9951 暴跌至 gold-eval 的 0.76（-21.9pp），直接量化了 circular evaluation\n      的膨胀效应。这是 median 档的核心预期：structural features ≈ LF inputs，所以在 LF labels 上近乎完美\n      是 artifact，但在 gold 上仍保持 0.76 说明结构信号有真实价值——不只是拟合 LF 规则。\n      0.76 落在 median 范围 [0.68, 0.83] 中间。Conf≥2 上 GB 表现更好（0.82）因为这些窗口 LF\n      本身 82% 正确，structural features 在这些\"LF 正确\"的子集上性能保持。\n      Conf=1 上 GB 降至 0.67 但仍高于 LF 自身准确率（0.51），说明 GB 学到了超越单 LF 规则的\n      smoother boundaries。RF 略低于 GB 因为 RF 的离散 splits 更容易过拟合 LF 的离散规则，\n      而 GB 的 gradient boosting 有更好的正则化泛化。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Structural Models on Gold vs LF Labels\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"LF-eval F1\", \"Gold-eval F1\", \"Δ (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Structural GB\", 0.9951, 0.76, -23.5]\n          - [\"Structural RF\", 0.9951, 0.74, -25.5]\n          - [\"Structural LR\", 0.9874, 0.73, -25.7]\n          - [\"Probe (GRU)\", 0.9055, 0.69, -21.6]\n          - [\"LLM-judge\", 0.6625, 0.60, -6.3]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Grouped bar chart: 每个模型在 LF-eval vs Gold-eval 上的 macro_f1（双色对比）\"\n      - \"Feature importance on gold: structural GB 的 top-10 features 对比 LF-eval 的 feature importance 变化\"\n    analysis: >\n      Circular eval 膨胀 ~22pp 是论文最重要的方法论发现之一。但 structural features 在 gold 上仍为最高分\n      （0.76 vs probe 0.69 vs LLM-judge 0.60），证明\"structural features dominate current approaches\"\n      这一降级后的 claim 成立。Feature importance 可能发生重排序：LF-eval 上 cmd_rep_ratio 最重要\n      （因为 cmd_rep LF 覆盖率 97.4%），但 gold-eval 上 file_diff 相关特征可能上升（因为 file activity\n      是更可靠的 cross-context 信号）。\n\n  # ── gold-set 子实验 4: Probe 在 gold 上评估 ──\n  - name: \"gold-probe-eval\"\n    plan_id: \"gold-set\"\n    description: >\n      GRU probe（probe_001 + multiseed + encoder variants）在 gold 标签上评估。\n      核心回答：embedding-based approach 在真实标签上的相对表现。\n    expected_results:\n      test_set: \"gold 650 windows\"\n      probe_001_qwen:\n        macro_f1: 0.69\n        accuracy: 0.72\n        f1_stag: 0.62\n        f1_prog: 0.76\n      probe_e5large:\n        macro_f1: 0.71\n        accuracy: 0.74\n        f1_stag: 0.65\n        f1_prog: 0.77\n      probe_bgem3:\n        macro_f1: 0.72\n        accuracy: 0.74\n        f1_stag: 0.66\n        f1_prog: 0.78\n      structural_minus_probe_gold_pp: 7\n      structural_minus_probe_lf_pp: 8.96\n      gap_narrowing_pp: 1.96\n      by_gold_confidence:\n        conf_ge2:\n          probe_001_macro_f1: 0.75\n        conf1:\n          probe_001_macro_f1: 0.61\n    result_rationale: >\n      Probe 从 LF-eval 0.9055 降至 gold-eval 0.69（-21.6pp）：probe 在 LF labels 上训练，\n      继承了 LF 偏差，gold 暴露了这些偏差。但 structural - probe gap 从 8.96pp（LF）缩窄到 7pp（gold），\n      落在 median 范围 [1, 8] 内。缩窄原因：probe 的 embedding 捕获了一些 structural features 无法编码的\n      语义信号（如 action 描述的语义相似度暗示逻辑循环），这些信号在 LF-eval 上被 circular eval 淹没，\n      但在 gold 上体现出微弱的额外价值。BGE-m3 在 gold 上表现最好（0.72 vs Qwen 0.69），\n      可能因为 BGE-m3 的多语言训练使其对 code-NL 混合文本的编码更鲁棒，捕获了更多 task-agnostic 语义信号。\n      但 7pp gap 仍然显著，证明\"structural features dominate current approaches\"成立。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Probe Variants on Gold Labels\"\n        columns: [\"Encoder\", \"LF-eval F1\", \"Gold-eval F1\", \"Δ vs Structural GB (gold)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-0.6B\", 0.9055, 0.69, \"-7pp\"]\n          - [\"E5-large-v2\", 0.9363, 0.71, \"-5pp\"]\n          - [\"BGE-m3\", 0.9413, 0.72, \"-4pp\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Encoder 比较 bar chart: 三个 encoder 在 LF-eval vs Gold-eval 上的 macro_f1\"\n      - \"Scatter plot: probe 预测概率 vs gold label，按 LF confidence 着色\"\n    analysis: >\n      Probe 在 gold 上表现弱于 structural（7pp gap），但 encoder 之间的排序反转值得注意：\n      LF-eval 上 Qwen/BGE/E5 差距小（±3.6pp），但 gold 上 BGE-m3 拉开优势。\n      这暗示 encoder 的泛化能力差异在 circular eval 中被压缩，gold 上才暴露。\n      Probe 的真实 contribution 不是超越 structural，而是提供 (a) end-to-end 部署路径，\n      (b) 在 conf=1 的语义歧义窗口上可能有互补价值（probe conf=1 F1=0.61 vs structural conf=1 F1=0.67，\n      差距仅 6pp，比 overall 差距 7pp 更小，暗示 probe 在歧义区域有相对优势）。\n\n  # ── gold-set 子实验 5: LLM-judge 在 gold 上评估 ──\n  - name: \"gold-llm-judge-eval\"\n    plan_id: \"gold-set\"\n    description: >\n      LLM-as-judge (Claude Sonnet, zero-shot) 在 gold 标签上评估。\n      核心回答：LLM-judge 对 LF labels 的\"disagreement\"中有多少是 correct human-aligned judgment？\n    expected_results:\n      test_set: \"gold 650 windows (same windows as LLM-judge baseline)\"\n      llm_judge_gold:\n        macro_f1: 0.60\n        accuracy: 0.63\n        f1_stag: 0.54\n        f1_prog: 0.66\n        precision_stag: 0.58\n        recall_stag: 0.50\n      llm_judge_lf_eval_ref:\n        macro_f1: 0.6625\n      delta_gold_vs_lf_pp: -6.3\n      structural_minus_llm_gold_pp: 16\n      probe_minus_llm_gold_pp: 9\n      llm_judge_correct_lf_wrong_pct: 8.2\n      llm_judge_wrong_lf_correct_pct: 14.5\n      llm_judge_both_wrong_pct: 6.1\n      by_gold_confidence:\n        conf_ge2:\n          llm_judge_macro_f1: 0.63\n        conf1:\n          llm_judge_macro_f1: 0.57\n    result_rationale: >\n      LLM-judge 从 LF-eval 0.6625 降至 gold-eval 0.60（-6.3pp），降幅远小于 structural（-22pp）\n      和 probe（-22pp）。这是因为 LLM-judge 本来就不拟合 LF labels，所以 circular eval 的去除\n      对它影响最小。但 LLM-judge 仍排最末（0.60），因为 zero-shot prompting 缺乏：\n      (a) 对 SWE-bench task 结构的先验知识（不知道什么 command pattern 意味着停滞），\n      (b) 窗口级时序 context（只看 5 步摘要，不理解 trajectory 动态），\n      (c) agent 架构特异性（不了解 SWE-Agent vs OpenHands 的行为模式）。\n      8.2% 的窗口上 LLM-judge 对而 LF 错——这些是 LLM 的\"语义理解\"正确捕获的案例，\n      但 14.5% 上 LLM 错而 LF 对，说明 LLM 的独立判断不够可靠。\n      Structural - LLM gap = 16pp 落在 median 范围 [5, 20] 中间，\n      证明 structural efficiency advantage survives 但 accuracy advantage 确实 weakens\n      （从 LF-eval 的 33pp 降到 gold 的 16pp）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: LLM-Judge Error Decomposition vs LF on Gold\"\n        columns: [\"Category\", \"Count\", \"% of 650\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Both correct\", 398, \"61.2%\"]\n          - [\"LLM correct, LF wrong\", 53, \"8.2%\"]\n          - [\"LLM wrong, LF correct\", 94, \"14.5%\"]\n          - [\"Both wrong\", 40, \"6.1%\"]\n          - [\"Ambiguous (adjudicated)\", 65, \"10.0%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: Structural vs Probe vs LLM-judge on gold macro_f1, 标注与 LF-eval 的 Δ\"\n      - \"Venn diagram: 三种方法在 gold 上的 correct predictions 重叠\"\n    analysis: >\n      LLM-judge \"correct but LF wrong\" 的 8.2% 窗口是宝贵的分析材料——这些是语义理解真正有价值的案例。\n      定性分析预期：这些窗口中 agent 在做\"看似活跃但语义空转\"的操作（多样命令、有 file edit，\n      但 edit 内容无效）。LLM 能读懂 edit 内容判断无效，而 LF 只看结构特征判定 progress。\n      然而 14.5% 的 \"LLM wrong, LF correct\" 表明 LLM 也有系统性偏差：\n      倾向于将 verbose output（长 error messages、详细 traceback）误判为 stagnation。\n\n  # ── gold-set 子实验 6: 时序动态在 gold 上的验证 ──\n  - name: \"gold-temporal-validation\"\n    plan_id: \"gold-set\"\n    description: >\n      在 gold 标注的 stagnation onset 边界上验证 LF temporal dynamics。\n      人类标注 stagnation 起始步，与 LF first-fire 步进行对齐分析。\n    expected_results:\n      gold_annotated_onsets: 270\n      onset_alignment:\n        within_1_step_pct: 32\n        within_2_steps_pct: 52\n        within_3_steps_pct: 64\n        mean_absolute_offset_steps: 2.8\n        median_absolute_offset_steps: 2.0\n        std_offset_steps: 2.1\n      by_lf:\n        cmd_rep:\n          mean_offset_vs_gold: -1.2\n          within_2_steps_pct: 48\n          note: \"fires before human-perceived onset, moderate alignment\"\n        file_diff:\n          mean_offset_vs_gold: -0.6\n          within_2_steps_pct: 56\n          note: \"most aligned with human onset, slightly early\"\n        outcome_bp:\n          mean_offset_vs_gold: 5.3\n          within_2_steps_pct: 22\n          note: \"fires well after human-perceived onset, by design\"\n      role_reversal_on_gold: >\n        Gold confirms cmd_rep leads on SWE-Agent (offset -1.2 vs gold) but temporal \n        role reversal on OH cannot be validated (no OH gold set in this batch).\n      onset_timing_noise_caveat: \"±2-3 step noise in onset alignment\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Overall onset alignment 52%（±2 步内）落在 median 范围 [40, 65] 中间。\n      低于 65% 因为：(a) 人类判断的 stagnation onset 本质是主观的（\"从哪一步开始不 productive\"\n      没有客观答案），(b) LFs 的 binary firing 是 threshold-based 的离散跳变，而人类感知的\n      onset 是渐进的，(c) OB（lagging LF）在 stagnation 已经发生很久后才 fire，拉低 average。\n      高于 40% 因为 cmd_rep 和 file_diff 作为 leading LFs，在多数 structural stagnation 案例上\n      确实在人类感知 onset 附近 fire。file_diff 对齐最好（56% within ±2），因为\"文件不再变化\"\n      是人类和 LF 共同认可的最直观 stagnation 信号。这支持 Claim 2 但需要加 caveat：\n      onset timing 是统计趋势（±2-3 步），不是精确预测工具。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: LF Onset Alignment with Gold Annotations\"\n        columns: [\"LF\", \"Mean Offset (steps)\", \"Within ±2 steps\", \"Within ±3 steps\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"cmd_rep\", -1.2, \"48%\", \"61%\"]\n          - [\"file_diff\", -0.6, \"56%\", \"68%\"]\n          - [\"outcome_bp\", +5.3, \"22%\", \"34%\"]\n          - [\"Any LF (first fire)\", -0.8, \"52%\", \"64%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Histogram: onset offset distribution (gold - LF first fire), 分 LF 着色\"\n      - \"Timeline visualization: 5 个 example trajectories 展示 gold onset vs LF fire 时间\"\n    analysis: >\n      cmd_rep 在 LF-eval 上 mean_lag=-1.87（relative to stag label onset），在 gold 上 offset=-1.2\n      （relative to human onset）——方向一致但幅度缩小。这是因为 LF-derived onset 定义比 human onset\n      更 sharp（binary threshold），而 gold onset 更渐进。\n      OB 在 gold 上 offset=+5.3（vs LF-eval 上 +6.7），缩小因为 gold-defined stagnation windows\n      通常更长（人类标注的 stagnation 包含了 LFs 未标记的\"尾部\"）。\n      关键 caveat：52% 的 ±2 步对齐意味着 onset prediction 只是粗略指示，不适合作为 intervention trigger。\n\n  # ── gold-set 子实验 7: 语义残差与错误分类学 ──\n  - name: \"gold-error-taxonomy\"\n    plan_id: \"gold-set\"\n    description: >\n      Gold set error analysis：识别 structural features 和 probe 都无法捕获的 stagnation 类型\n      （\"语义残差\"），构建 stagnation 类型分类学。\n    expected_results:\n      total_gold_stagnation: 270\n      structural_correct_stag: 192\n      structural_missed_stag: 78\n      structural_recall_stag: 0.71\n      missed_stag_taxonomy:\n        strategic_dead_end:\n          count: 31\n          pct_of_missed: 39.7\n          description: >\n            Agent 追求连贯但根本错误的方法。命令多样、有 file edit，但方向错误。\n            只有理解 task goal 的人才能判断。cmd_rep 不 fire（命令不重复），\n            file_diff 不 fire（确实在改文件），OB 可能 fire 也可能不 fire。\n          structural_f1: 0.22\n          probe_f1: 0.28\n          llm_judge_f1: 0.38\n        implicit_repetition:\n          count: 24\n          pct_of_missed: 30.8\n          description: >\n            Agent 用不同语法/命令表达相同逻辑尝试。字面 cmd_rep 低，但语义重复高。\n            如：先 grep 搜索，再 find 搜索，再 ag 搜索——命令不同但意图相同。\n          structural_f1: 0.31\n          probe_f1: 0.35\n          llm_judge_f1: 0.33\n        unfocused_exploration:\n          count: 23\n          pct_of_missed: 29.5\n          description: >\n            Agent 快速切换多种方法但都不 viable。结构上看像 productive exploration\n            （命令多样、文件变化频繁），但实际是无方向的 thrashing。\n          structural_f1: 0.18\n          probe_f1: 0.24\n          llm_judge_f1: 0.30\n      semantic_residual_total: 78\n      semantic_residual_pct_of_gold_stag: 28.9\n      probe_captures_partial_pct: 12.3\n      llm_captures_partial_pct: 18.7\n      neither_captures_pct: 22.6\n    result_rationale: >\n      78/270（28.9%）的 gold stagnation 构成\"语义残差\"——structural features 系统性 miss。\n      这些 stagnation 类型有共同特征：结构信号看起来像 progress（命令多样、有 file edit、\n      不触发 LF 阈值）。三种子类型反映不同的失败模式：\n      (1) strategic_dead_end（39.7%）是最大类：agent 一条路走到黑，结构上完全正常，\n      只有理解 task intent 才能判断。LLM-judge 在这类上最好（0.38）因为它能部分理解 intent；\n      (2) implicit_repetition（30.8%）：语义层面的重复，但 cmd_rep LF 的 literal matching 抓不到。\n      Probe embedding 理论上能捕获语义相似度但实际没有，因为 embedding 编码的是 step-level 文本\n      而非 action-level intent；\n      (3) unfocused_exploration（29.5%）：结构特征最难的一类，因为高活跃度被误判为 progress。\n      28.9% 的语义残差为 Claim 1 降级提供精确量化：structural features 捕获 71% 的真实 stagnation，\n      但遗漏 29%。这不是 marginal gap——是结构方法论的固有 ceiling。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: Stagnation Type Taxonomy on Gold Set\"\n        columns: [\"Type\", \"Count\", \"% of Gold Stag\", \"Struct F1\", \"Probe F1\", \"LLM F1\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Repetitive-structural (LFs capture)\", 146, \"54.1%\", 0.88, 0.79, 0.58]\n          - [\"Low-activity stagnation (LFs capture)\", 46, \"17.0%\", 0.83, 0.72, 0.55]\n          - [\"Strategic dead-end (semantic)\", 31, \"11.5%\", 0.22, 0.28, 0.38]\n          - [\"Implicit repetition (semantic)\", 24, \"8.9%\", 0.31, 0.35, 0.33]\n          - [\"Unfocused exploration (semantic)\", 23, \"8.5%\", 0.18, 0.24, 0.30]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: stagnation type × method performance (structural / probe / LLM)\"\n      - \"Example windows: 每种 semantic residual 类型展示 1-2 个代表性 trajectory 片段\"\n      - \"Venn diagram: structural / probe / LLM 在 gold stagnation 上的 coverage overlap\"\n    analysis: >\n      语义残差的存在证明 Claim 1 的原始表述（\"signals ARE structural\"）过强。修正为：\n      \"LF-approximated stagnation 是 structural 的；但 human-recognizable stagnation 有额外的\n      语义维度，当前所有自动方法（structural、NL probe、LLM-judge）都未有效捕获。\"\n      重要的是：probe 和 LLM-judge 在语义残差上也表现很差（F1 0.24-0.38），说明当前 NL 方法\n      同样无法捕获语义残差——这支持\"structural features dominate CURRENT approaches\"的降级 claim，\n      同时为 future work 打开空间（需要 task-aware semantic understanding）。\n\n  # ── f1-stag-analysis ──\n  - name: \"f1-stag-per-class-breakdown\"\n    plan_id: \"f1-stag-analysis\"\n    description: >\n      在现有 LF-derived test set (N=1824) 上对 F1_stag 按多维度拆分：\n      trajectory 位置、dominant LF、置信度、trajectory outcome。\n      补充 gold set 上的同维度拆分（如可用）。\n    expected_results:\n      test_set_lf: \"conf≥2, N=1824, 485 stag / 1339 prog\"\n      overall_f1_stag: 0.8593\n      by_trajectory_position:\n        early_0_33:\n          n_stag: 98\n          f1_stag: 0.88\n          note: \"stagnation in early trajectory = usually clear repetitive pattern\"\n        middle_33_66:\n          n_stag: 132\n          f1_stag: 0.79\n          note: \"hardest segment — transitional states, boundary ambiguity\"\n        late_66_100:\n          n_stag: 255\n          f1_stag: 0.87\n          note: \"late stagnation usually well-established pattern\"\n      by_dominant_lf:\n        cmd_rep_dominant:\n          n_stag: 291\n          f1_stag: 0.90\n          note: \"cmd_rep signal strong and clean, probe easily learns\"\n        file_diff_dominant:\n          n_stag: 108\n          f1_stag: 0.83\n          note: \"file inactivity signal moderate, some false negatives\"\n        ob_dominant:\n          n_stag: 42\n          f1_stag: 0.72\n          note: \"OB-only stagnation hardest — lagging signal creates boundary noise\"\n        multi_signal:\n          n_stag: 44\n          f1_stag: 0.94\n          note: \"all LFs agree — easiest cases\"\n      by_confidence:\n        conf2:\n          n_stag: 463\n          f1_stag: 0.86\n        conf3:\n          n_stag: 22\n          f1_stag: 0.91\n      by_trajectory_outcome:\n        resolved:\n          n_stag: 8\n          f1_stag: 0.94\n          note: \"resolved trajectories have clear stag→progress transition\"\n        unresolved:\n          n_stag: 477\n          f1_stag: 0.85\n      gold_set_breakdown_if_available:\n        overall_f1_stag_gold: 0.62\n        by_type:\n          structural_stagnation: 0.78\n          semantic_stagnation: 0.27\n        by_position:\n          early: 0.68\n          middle: 0.55\n          late: 0.64\n    result_rationale: >\n      F1_stag 拆分揭示 probe 性能的非均匀分布。Middle segment 最差（0.79）因为 trajectory 中段\n      经常出现\"尝试新方向\"vs\"继续停滞\"的模糊过渡，probe 的 window-level 分类无法准确捕获\n      这种渐变。cmd_rep-dominant stagnation 最容易（0.90），因为 embedding 中的 token repetition\n      pattern 最易被 GRU 学习。OB-dominant 最难（0.72）因为 OB 是 lagging signal，\n      stagnation window 的 OB fire 来自未来的 outcome 信息，probe 在 inference 时看不到 outcome。\n      Multi-signal stagnation 最高（0.94）因为 all-3-agree 的窗口标签最干净、pattern 最一致。\n      Gold set 上 overall F1_stag 预期 0.62，远低于 LF-eval 的 0.86——semantic stagnation\n      类型（F1=0.27）大幅拉低整体。这是 Claim 1 降级的具体量化证据。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table: F1_stag Breakdown by Dimension (LF Test Set)\"\n        columns: [\"Dimension\", \"Subcategory\", \"N_stag\", \"F1_stag\", \"Δ vs Overall\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Position\", \"Early (0-33%)\", 98, 0.88, \"+2.1pp\"]\n          - [\"Position\", \"Middle (33-66%)\", 132, 0.79, \"-6.9pp\"]\n          - [\"Position\", \"Late (66-100%)\", 255, 0.87, \"+1.1pp\"]\n          - [\"Dominant LF\", \"cmd_rep\", 291, 0.90, \"+4.1pp\"]\n          - [\"Dominant LF\", \"file_diff\", 108, 0.83, \"-2.9pp\"]\n          - [\"Dominant LF\", \"outcome_bp\", 42, 0.72, \"-13.9pp\"]\n          - [\"Dominant LF\", \"multi-signal\", 44, 0.94, \"+8.1pp\"]\n          - [\"Outcome\", \"Resolved\", 8, 0.94, \"+8.1pp\"]\n          - [\"Outcome\", \"Unresolved\", 477, 0.85, \"-0.9pp\"]\n      - name: \"Table: F1_stag on Gold by Stagnation Type (if gold available)\"\n        columns: [\"Stagnation Type\", \"N\", \"Probe F1_stag\", \"Structural F1_stag\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Structural (LF-capturable)\", 192, 0.78, 0.88]\n          - [\"Strategic dead-end\", 31, 0.22, 0.16]\n          - [\"Implicit repetition\", 24, 0.30, 0.25]\n          - [\"Unfocused exploration\", 23, 0.19, 0.12]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: F1_stag across position × dominant-LF (2D grid，颜色深浅表示 F1)\"\n      - \"Box plot: per-trajectory F1_stag 分布，按 trajectory outcome 分组\"\n      - \"Bar chart: LF-eval F1_stag vs Gold-eval F1_stag 对比（如 gold 可用）\"\n    analysis: >\n      F1_stag 的维度拆分提供三个关键 insights：\n      (1) OB-dominant stagnation（F1=0.72）是最大 weakness——这些窗口的 stagnation 信号\n      主要来自未来的 task outcome 而非当前 window 内容，probe 在 real-time inference 中无法利用；\n      (2) Middle-segment 低 F1（0.79）揭示 window-level 分类的固有局限：\n      stagnation onset/offset 的渐变过渡被 binary classification 强制离散化；\n      (3) Gold set 上的拆分（如可用）将把 structural vs semantic stagnation 的性能差距\n      精确量化：structural stagnation F1=0.78 vs semantic stagnation F1=0.27，\n      确认 ~29% 的 stagnation 是当前方法论的 blind spot。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"dcbc9989-a384-4059-b23d-1b456a845b92","total_cost_usd":0.75564575,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31579,"cache_read_input_tokens":54930,"output_tokens":20179,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31579,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":20021,"cache_read_input_tokens":43089,"cache_creation_input_tokens":331,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":331},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":26217,"outputTokens":21,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.026322,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":3,"outputTokens":20179,"cacheReadInputTokens":54930,"cacheCreationInputTokens":31579,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7293237499999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"ab62b2a2-1b9a-43df-bbc5-0c130a9c63d8"}
